abstract: >-
  Article, exact-arithmetic certificates, PARI/GP and Python replay checks and
  Lean 4 sources for the theorem that F_N(A)-1 is not an integer square when
  A is congruent to 2 modulo 4 and N > 0 is divisible by 17 or 41, in the
  family F_0(A)=1, F_1(A)=A, F_{n+2}(A)=2A F_{n+1}(A)+F_n(A), with an
  application to the exact Pell exponent in a square-middle powerful-number
  family. The article text, explanatory guide and data are CC BY 4.0; the
  code is Apache-2.0. The human Hilbert-reciprocity proof is not itself Lean
  formalised; the Lean development covers the integer-Jacobi and recurrence
  exclusions and their propagation. No DOI or arXiv identifier is assigned at
  this version.
